{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Real-time visualization of MIDI Continuous Controller (CC) messages with two display modes: a scrolling time graph and current-value bars, plus performance metrics for hardware testing and technique analysis (events/s, rate, jitter).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each CC number is tracked per MIDI channel, so the same CC from different channels is displayed and measured separately.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Slider 1 selects the CC to monitor (0 = all CCs); slider 3 sets the time window in seconds (1-30). Metrics are computed over a 1-second window, filtered on read, so the numbers describe exactly the second they claim to.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each (CC, channel) pair has its own colour shade, the bars carry it in the label, the time axis is labelled, and Freeze stops the acquisition so a reading can be examined without it moving.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The three numbers per pair are named after what they mean, not after how they are computed: Messages = how many times per second the controller sends; Motion = how far the value travels per second (gesture speed); Timing = how much the spacing between messages wobbles. Pointing at them says the same thing on screen.\par}
}
